  "batteryHelpTitle": "Battery, alarms and pinning",
  "batteryHelpAlarmsTitle": "Alarms on time",
  "batteryHelpAlarmsBody": "Kid Timer asks the system to ring at the end of the timer, even with the app closed or the screen locked. For that it needs permission to show notifications and, on Android, the \"Alarms & reminders\" permission.",
  "batteryHelpAlarmsApple": "On iPhone, iPad and Mac: Settings › Notifications › Kid Timer › turn on Allow Notifications and Time Sensitive.",
  "batteryHelpOpenExactAlarm": "Open alarms & reminders",
  "batteryHelpOpenNotifications": "Open notification settings",
  "batteryHelpBatteryTitle": "Battery optimization",
  "batteryHelpBatteryBody": "Some phones close apps in the background to save battery, which can delay the alarm. Let Kid Timer run without restrictions:",
  "batteryHelpBatterySamsung": "Samsung: Settings › Apps › Kid Timer › Battery › Unrestricted.",
  "batteryHelpBatteryXiaomi": "Xiaomi, Redmi, POCO: Settings › Apps › Manage apps › Kid Timer › Battery saver › No restrictions, and turn on Autostart.",
  "batteryHelpBatteryMotorola": "Motorola: Settings › Apps › Kid Timer › App battery usage › Unrestricted.",
  "batteryHelpBatteryHuawei": "Huawei: Settings › Battery › App launch › Kid Timer › Manage manually, with Auto-launch and Run in background on.",
  "batteryHelpBatteryOthers": "Others: Settings › Apps › Kid Timer › Battery › Unrestricted (or Don't optimize).",
  "batteryHelpOpenBatteryOptimization": "Open battery optimization",
  "batteryHelpPinningTitle": "Keep the child in the app",
  "batteryHelpPinningAndroid": "Android: turn on Settings › Security › App pinning, then pin Kid Timer from the recent apps screen.",
  "batteryHelpPinningApple": "iPhone and iPad: turn on Settings › Accessibility › Guided Access, then triple-click the side button inside Kid Timer.",
  "batteryHelpPinningDesktop": "Computers: use full screen with the child lock on.",
  "batteryHelpWebTitle": "Why keep the window open",
  "batteryHelpWebBody": "Browsers and Linux don't let apps schedule alarms with the system. Kid Timer plays the alarm itself, so it only rings while the window or tab is open and the computer is awake."
